or links the gated evidence to the landed commit.

## Closing the epic needs the same re-scope this bead got

`etude-9uf`'s own acceptance says the supervisor advances each phase with a
single `etude gate` invocation that runs the tier's seats live and records the
attempt. **This run did not meet that**, and could not: `etude gate` passed 0 of
5, and every pass required a manual append.

`etude-9uf.5` re-scoped its acceptance explicitly, in `bd`, before the run.
Closing the epic requires the same treatment — its wording amended on the tracked
record to what the model actually does today, pointing at `etude-4ed` for the
part that remains undone. Closing it silently against unmet wording would be the
epic's own target defect, committed on the way out the door.

